## Context

Author direction (2026-06-06, 0446 review): "Code can be parametrized by
experiment. Also produce the exp2 versions (four arms)." 0446 delivered the
model-list parametrization (`--models` / `--exclude-models` on
`aedist.plot_exp1_matrix`, with `strong` and `top` cohort versions wired in
render.mk). Experiment parametrization is a separate lift: Exp2 records live
in the exp2 mart layer (`exp2_mart.jsonl` / mart views), carry an *arm*
dimension (naive comparator vs optimized × agents), and the per-run plant
lists come out of a different derivation than
`aedist.exp1_recognition.load_exp1_recognition` (which globs exp1_batch2
record.json files).

## Quoi faire

1. Generalize the recognition derivation: either extend `exp1_recognition`
   with an exp2 loader producing the same `RecognitionCell` /
   `fp_presence` contract, or add a sibling `exp2_recognition` module on the
   mart layer (respect the render-DAG rule: figures read their own mart
   view, no P3-to-P3 side-outputs, cf. 0436).
2. One matrix per arm (four figures), same layout as the Exp1 matrix
   (lifecycle band order, model rows, FP panel recomputed per arm).
3. Wire in render.mk (one output per rule) under `chart-figures`.
4. Decide with the author where (if anywhere) they land in the manuscript —
   exploration artifacts first.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Four arm-specific matrix PDFs build from the mart layer via the DAG
- [ ] Same visual conventions as the Exp1 matrix (0446 layout)
- [ ] `make check-fast` + `pytest -m adherence` green
- [ ] Author review of the four figures

## Related

- 0446 (Exp1 matrix rework — layout and parametrization base)
- 0436 (render DAG: no P3-to-P3 side-output edges)
- 0171 (Phase C cross-eval — same four-arm structure, journal delta)
